      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/nquads-distribution.svg",
      "description": "Extract, partition, package, and distribute knowledge graph datasets as W3C RDF 1.1 N-Quads with pre-compiled named SPARQL queries. Governed by skills `nquads-distribution` and `named-query-execution`, grounded in `schemas/kg/nquads-distribution.ts`.\n\nCRITICAL INVARIANTS:\n1. 2-TIER SUBGRAPH ARCHITECTURE: A lightweight Spine backbone partition is loaded on startup, while bulky subgraphs (communities, workflow domains) are lazily fetched on demand.\n2. UPSTREAM SKOLEMIZATION: Zero blank nodes across all partitions. Every node must carry a deterministic minted IRI.\n3. PARTITION BUDGET CEILING: Partitions must strictly stay under 5 MB gzipped / 50k quads to protect browser heap and memory allocations.\n4. GRAPH AVAILABILITY GUARD: Queries declare requiredSubgraphs; execution fails fast with MissingPartitionError rather than silently returning partial query results.\n5. NO COMMITTED BINARY PAYLOADS: `.nq.gz` distribution payloads are gitignored, generated on demand or in CI, and served to Pages via 'served: true'.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 12,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/directory/kg-ops",
      "name": "Package and distribute partitioned W3C N-Quads and named queries",
